From e24b790d057968cae750e697f0b419378f285627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YahiaAngelo <yahia.mostafa.elsayed@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:32:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] tcg: recycle the oldest code regions when the buffer is
 full (VPHONE_TB_RECYCLE)

When the code buffer is full, QEMU flushes every TB. The iPhone guest fills
the 2 GiB buffer every 1-2 minutes during boot and app launches (median TB 2
guest instructions, ~400 host bytes), and 33-50% of its translations then
redo TBs the flush threw away.

With VPHONE_TB_RECYCLE=1 (or arm 1 of VPHONE_AB_WHAT=tb_recycle) the safe
work queued on a full buffer instead invalidates the TBs of the oldest
quarter of the regions (by allocation order, never a translation context's
current one) with tb_phys_invalidate, clears the indirect-branch-cache and
return-TB pointers of surviving TBs that point into them, flushes every jump
cache (which also outdates the RAS), and hands the regions out again. Other
flushes (A/B switch, gdbstub, ...) stay full flushes. Off by default.

Boot + app phases on the Duo: 19 recycles of a quarter buffer, 13.8M TBs
invalidated, apps render; translation cycles/s at boot 2.57G -> 1.96G, app
launches 1.74G -> 1.03G (different runs). tests/tcg/vphone-* pass with it on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N89PWg24VJrcxX3MuUo4uM
